---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";

/**
 * The privacy notice for the APP's closed beta (beta.present-the-app.com), as
 * opposed to /privacy/, which covers this website only. The app's landing page,
 * its AI consent screen and its settings link here.
 *
 * Every statement must stay true of the present-the-app/present repository and
 * the gitops.present deployment. When the app starts collecting something new,
 * this page changes in the same week, with the date below.
 */
const UPDATED = "19 November 2026";
const mail = site.contactEmail;
---

<Base
  title="App privacy"
  description="What the Present beta app collects, why, who processes it and how to delete it."
>
  <Prose
    title="App privacy"
    updated={`Last updated ${UPDATED}`}
    intro="This notice covers the Present app during its closed beta, at beta.present-the-app.com. This website has its own notice."
  >
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      We keep what you put into the app so it can work: your account, the quizzes you
      take about people, the gift ideas they produce, your wishlists and your dates.
      To suggest gifts, the quiz answers (never the person's name, or yours) go to
      our AI provider. We sell nothing, show no ads and use no third-party
      analytics. You can delete your account and everything in it from the app's
      settings at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      Present is a small independent project run from Switzerland. For anything about
      your data, write to <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What we keep, and why</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your account</strong>: email address, a hash of your password (never the
        password itself), your name if you give one, your birthday as a day and month
        if you add one (never the year), and passkeys or two-step sign-in if you set
        them up. To let you sign in.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your access request</strong>: the email address you asked for beta
        access with, and whether it was approved. To run the invitation.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Quizzes and ideas</strong>: the name you give the person, your answers
        (as choices from our lists, plus any favourites you type), and the gift ideas
        generated from them. To show them back to you and improve later suggestions.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Wishlists, saved ideas, dates and connections</strong>: what you add.
        When you share a wishlist, anyone with its link can see it, and someone who
        reserves an item can leave a first name, which they can remove again.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Signed-in devices</strong>: for each session, the device's browser
        description and IP address, so you can see and end your sessions in
        settings. Expired sessions are deleted every night.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Usage counts</strong>: which steps of the app were used (for example
        "a quiz was finished", "an idea was saved"), from a fixed list, with no
        content. Feedback you choose to send us, and error reports from the app,
        which are stripped of their content before they are kept. To find out what
        works during the beta.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your AI consent</strong>: a record that you accepted, and which
        version of the text you saw. It is kept after account deletion in hashed form,
        because it is our proof that we asked.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We ask you not to type private details about anyone (health, religion and so
      on). The quiz never asks for them.
    </p>

    <h2>The AI that suggests gifts</h2>
    <p>
      Gift ideas are written by an AI model from <strong>Anthropic</strong> (Anthropic
      PBC, United States). Only after you accept the consent screen, each time you ask
      for ideas we send the quiz answers: the occasion, the budget, the interests,
      style and gift taste you picked, and any favourites you typed. We never send the
      person's name, your name, your email or anything else that identifies either of
      you. Anthropic processes this for us under its commercial terms, which do not
      allow it to train its models on what we send.
    </p>

    <h2>Who else processes data for us</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare</strong> carries traffic to the app and runs the anti-bot
        check on the access form. It sees your IP address and the pages you request.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Resend</strong> sends the app's emails (your invitation, password
        resets). It receives your email address and the message.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Openverse</strong> and the sites it points to supply some of the
        illustration photos on gift ideas. Your browser loads those images directly,
        so those sites see your IP address. We send them only the gift's search words.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The app and its database run on servers in Switzerland that we operate
      ourselves. Anthropic, Cloudflare and Resend are based in the United States; data
      sent to them leaves Switzerland under the safeguards each of them provides for
      such transfers.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      For as long as your account exists. Deleting your account in settings removes
      your account and everything in it straight away, except the consent record
      above. Server logs and backups roll over within three months.
    </p>

    <h2>Age</h2>
    <p>The app is for people aged 13 and over.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask what we hold about you, have it corrected or deleted, or receive a
      copy. Most of this you can do yourself in the app; for the rest, write to
      <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>. You can also complain to the Swiss
      Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner (FDPIC).
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this changes in a way that matters, the date at the top changes with it, and
      we tell testers by email.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
